    "summary": "US Secretary of State Marco Rubio called on Ethiopia and Eritrea to respect the sovereignty and territorial integrity of neighboring countries, warning against cross-border actions that could escalate regional tensions.",
    "content": "US Secretary of State Marco Rubio held a telephone conversation with Ethiopian Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed on Wednesday, during which he urged Ethiopia and Eritrea to respect the sovereignty and territorial integrity of neighboring countries in the Horn of Africa. According to a State Department statement, Rubio emphasized the need to avoid cross-border actions that could further inflame regional conflicts.\n\nThe call comes amid heightened tensions in the Horn of Africa, particularly over Ethiopia's pursuit of sea access, which has raised concerns in Eritrea and other neighboring states. Ethiopia, a landlocked country, has sought to secure a port through diplomatic or other means, leading to fears of potential military confrontation. The United States has been closely monitoring the situation and engaging with regional leaders to prevent escalation.\n\nRubio and Abiy also discussed broader regional stability and bilateral relations between the United States and Ethiopia. The State Department described the conversation as part of ongoing diplomatic efforts to promote peace and security in the region. Neither side provided further details on specific commitments made during the call.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this development is significant because any conflict between Ethiopia and Eritrea could destabilize the wider Horn of Africa, affecting Somalia's security and political landscape. Somalia has already faced decades of instability, and renewed tensions between its neighbors could exacerbate existing challenges, including the fight against al-Shabaab and the fragile state-building process. The diaspora, which maintains strong ties to the region, has a vested interest in seeing de-escalation and respect for international borders.\n\nThis intervention by the United States underscores the international community's concern about the potential for a new conflict in a region already grappling with multiple crises. It also highlights the strategic importance of the Horn of Africa to global powers. The diaspora will be watching closely to see whether Rubio's message leads to tangible steps to reduce tensions and uphold the sovereignty of all states in the region.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/10/15/mareykanka-oo-itoobiya-iyo-eritrea-ugu-baaqay-ixtiraamka-madax-bannaanida-dalalka-gobolka/",
