    "original_title": "Ra’iisul Wasaare Xamse Sheegay inuu Kamid ahaa Dadkii ka Badbaaday Qaraxii Soobe",
    "slug": "somali-pm-reveals-he-survived-2017-mogadishu-truck-bombing",
    "summary": "Prime Minister Hamza Abdi Barre discloses he was near the scene of the October 14, 2017 Soobe junction attack and narrowly escaped, as Somalia marks the anniversary of the deadliest bombing in its history.",
    "content": "Somali Prime Minister Hamza Abdi Barre has revealed that he was among those who narrowly survived the massive truck bombing at the Soobe junction in Mogadishu on October 14, 2017. The attack, one of the deadliest in Somalia's history, killed hundreds and injured many more. In a statement, the Prime Minister said he was in a house near the site of the explosion when the bomb detonated.\n\nThe 2017 Soobe bombing remains a painful chapter for Somalia. A truck loaded with explosives exploded at a busy intersection, causing widespread destruction and loss of life. The attack was attributed to the militant group Al-Shabaab, though the group never formally claimed responsibility. The scale of the devastation overwhelmed hospitals and left families grieving across the nation.\n\nPrime Minister Hamza Abdi Barre, who took office in June 2022, has not previously spoken publicly about his personal experience that day. His account adds a new perspective to the national tragedy, highlighting the indiscriminate nature of terrorism. The Prime Minister noted that the house he was in suffered significant damage, underscoring how close he came to being a victim.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, the anniversary of the Soobe bombing is a time of collective mourning and reflection. Many in the diaspora lost relatives or friends in the attack, and the event continues to shape discussions about security and rebuilding efforts. The Prime Minister's disclosure may deepen the emotional connection for diaspora members, seeing a national leader share in their trauma.\n\nAs Somalia continues to confront security challenges, the Prime Minister's remarks serve as a reminder of the resilience required to rebuild. The government has repeatedly vowed to defeat Al-Shabaab and prevent future attacks. However, the memory of Soobe remains a stark symbol of the long road ahead.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/10/14/raiisul-wasaare-xamse-sheegay-inuu-kamid-ahaa-dadkii-ka-badbaaday-qaraxii-soobe/",
